ual decision-making is expected to be carried \nout by the actual stakeholders of an institution. \nE. Project Description, Scope and Management Milestones	2026-07-31 03:32:55.336635
86	12	14	14 \n \n1. Project Description \nThe project requires designing and developing a web-based, centralized, and decision support \nsystem for a simulated college setting. The simulated college setting comprises Operational \nAcademic Units and Parent Regulatory and Administrative Departments. The system aims at \ncapturing, storing, and reusing knowledge for decision-making in the academic and \nadministrative fields for the purpose of decision-making in the long run. The solution that has \nbeen proposed for the project is a knowledge management solution that utilizes a hybrid model \nfor knowledge management, which combines Knowledge Graph, structured databases, and \nRetrieval Augmented Generation. \n \nThe process starts with the inputting of the decision-related inputs in the form of the decision \nproblem, which means it is in the context of the constraint or the supporting document. The \ninputs that have already been fed into the system are encoded and stored in different data stores. \nThese data stores include the structured SQL data store, the graph data store for the semantic \nrelationships, and the text embeddings vector data store. The process of decision-making \ninvolves the processing of the user queries. This is done by the large language model, which \nrefines the queries and forwards them to the relevant data streams. The knowledge retrieved is \nthen unwound and fed back into the large language model for the creation of grounded and \ncontext-sensitive responses. \n \nThe target users of the system are the administrators of the college, the department heads, and the \nacademic planners. The users are benefited by the fact that the system allows them access to the \ndecisions made in the past by the university in natural language. \n2. Project Scope \nPlatform and Users \n \nThe project will provide a web-based platform which will be located in a simulated college. The \nsimulated college will consist of Operational Academic Units such as Business Administration \nDepartment, Information Technology Department, Management Department, Social Sciences \nDepartment, Hospitality Department, and Parent Regulatory and Administrative Department \nwhich includes Finance Department, Human Resource Department, and Quality Assurance and \nAccreditation Office. The users of the project will be academic administrators who can interact \nwith the system via a web browser interface. \n \nTechnology Stack \n \nThe application utilizes a state-of-the-art, high-performance stack, with the frontend implemented \nwith React, TypeScript, and the Vite framework, along with Zustand for state management, \nTanStack Query for data fetching and caching, and Tailwind CSS for rapid UI development, while	2026-07-31 03:33:08.709955
