96	12	20	20 \n \n \nFigure 3 : Gantt Chart of Milestone and Deliverables \nThe Gantt chart depicts the entire activity of the project from January 2026 to August 2026, \nincluding the order of activities, time period, and overlapping of the key activities of Capstone 1 \nand Capstone 2. From the figure, it is clear that there is a necessity for the first stage of the \nproject, which is aimed at the project start-up activities such as group development, topic \nnarrowing, proposal defense, and submission. The activities of this stage provide the base of the \nproject. \n \nThe milestones of Capstone 1 include requirement analysis, system architecture design, \nknowledge graph modeling, database schema development, and the first frontend and backend. \nThis stage is aimed at the idea design and implementation to ensure all the technical aspects are \ncorrect before the development on a large scale can take place. \n \nThe process of implementing, integrating, and evaluating the project is referred to as the \ncapstone 2 process. The major activities in this process include the implementation of the \nknowledge graph, the implementation of the retrieval augmented generation and the integration \nof the large language model, the implementation of the frontend features, the integration of the \nsystems, and the performance test of the system based on the simulated data sets provided. The \nfinal milestone activities include documentation, reporting, and presentation of the project. In	2026-07-31 03:34:03.834418
