236	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	69	document_chunk	0	B. Executive Summary \nEducational institutions increasingly rely on complex strategic and operational decisions made \nby academic leaders and administrators. Over time, the rationale, context, and outcomes of these \ndecisions are often lost due to staff turnover, fragmented documentation, and dependence on tacit \nknowledge. This erosion of institutional memory results in inconsistent decision making, \nrepeated errors, and limited organizational learning. Existing decision support systems in higher \neducation largely depend on static reports and structured data, which restricts their ability to \ncapture contextual relationships and support evidence-based reasoning over time.	[0.035355993,0.038913853,-0.16294801,-0.021408953,0.0873006,0.036441725,0.04156746,0.028692223,0.06676944,0.031973924,0.015262891,-0.011341266,0.108948685,0.054092836,0.01030655,-0.04089116,-0.0038212505,-0.028608467,-0.03156602,0.04132785,0.023283623,-0.025032014,-0.03713751,0.0058780853,0.033413872,0.04205884,0.006393343,-0.029723922,-0.05332381,0.022018492,0.049733046,0.041321453,0.03925148,-0.037783608,-0.062236972,-0.053029347,0.03748205,-0.0006779284,0.020946166,-0.024755964,-0.02970059,0.009551881,-0.004110401,-0.044285044,0.04883603,0.02662165,0.018877447,-0.026655028,0.039980803,-0.019259244,0.0114679895,-0.025562959,-0.0135852,0.02196796,0.016794963,0.008574137,-0.016000135,0.05186103,0.08086285,-0.07188637,0.11261393,0.059183788,-0.046922445,0.05361409,0.047271337,-0.015678313,-0.037430163,0.051732313,-0.022741666,-0.01611387,0.029787954,-0.009607275,0.013119786,-0.0120202815,-0.05910135,0.02455262,-0.013763122,-0.03548593,0.014657361,0.068846345,0.029842801,-0.024063319,0.08162833,-0.0019056596,0.055242535,0.055014696,0.0012505965,-0.0020180403,-0.0041238167,0.077471815,0.017306501,0.048842523,0.016947467,0.03872481,-0.082762346,0.02634246,-0.02129316,0.0048934706,-0.019151784,-0.026886666,-0.06039548,-0.040502504,-0.008308629,-0.03561449,