243	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	72	document_chunk	0	There have been many studies trying to improve the Decision Support Systems (DSS), through \nthe addition of structured decision-making models. In one study published in 2023, researchers \nused the Simple Additive Weighting (SAW) technique in the educational version of a DSS that \ncan help solve multiple criteria decision-making (MCDM). This DSS was evaluated by \ncomparing MCDM decisions made using methodologies with DSS against MCDM with no DSS. \nThe study concluded that DSS that include structured decision-making methodologies provide a \nclearer and more accurate outcome than an MCDM without DSS.(Hak, et al., 2023) \n1.2.5 Predictive Decision Support Systems Using Educational Data Mining \nThere have been many studies trying to improve the Decision Support Systems (DSS), through \nthe addition of structured decision-making models. In one study published in 2023, researchers \nused the Simple Additive Weighting (SAW) technique in the educational version of a DSS that \ncan help solve multiple criteria decision-making (MCDM). This DSS was evaluated by \ncomparing MCDM decisions made using methodologies with DSS against MCDM with no DSS. \nThe study concluded that DSS that include structured decision-making methodologies provide a \nclearer and more accurate outcome than an MCDM without DSS.(Saa, 2016)	[0.027744237,0.04333391,-0.159952,-0.04607721,0.060024492,-0.008357052,0.051315673,0.023122108,0.020755125,-0.016678324,0.017445363,0.0235272,0.15030307,0.066989586,-0.03412266,-0.013299964,-0.045891184,-0.07456353,-0.016541427,0.035853937,-0.05089604,-0.037351392,-0.043529097,0.00071983406,0.02786959,0.013359609,-0.052944195,0.012586738,-0.046352014,0.036155146,0.054019243,-0.011426912,0.0522122,-0.021695597,-0.09606041,-0.05526462,0.09720551,0.012146274,-0.022484707,-0.029366871,0.0023780847,0.0060336227,0.014830744,-0.035076078,0.047738485,-0.035526905,0.08161552,-0.048925146,0.05164069,-0.008117077,-0.0060246205,-0.052664