255	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	74	document_chunk	3	Linking Knowledge Graphs to RAG can create business opportunities. Previous studies show \nthat using knowledge graphs with RAG improves how well information is found and how \naccurate responses are. For example, the IKEDS framework achieved an accuracy rate of 85.7 \npercent in financial, health, and supply chain decisions by combining structured knowledge with \ngenerative capabilities (Wang, 2025). ). Similarly, KG2RAG discovered that using knowledge-\ngraph-based expansion and reorganization led to better retrieval F1 scores, increasing from 0.357 \nto 0.436 compared to retrieval using semantics (Zhu, 2025).Combining both methods shows \nconnections between retrieved content at the fact level, which makes answers more logical and \nrelevant to the context. These methods are often used for information access in general, and they \ncan also assist with retrieval and providing necessary responses. A lot of time is spent keeping up \nwith and rediscovering organizational decision-making information, where past knowledge, \nconnections, and outcomes are crucial for future decisions.	[0.01876295,0.07116734,-0.19847202,-0.06674487,0.06834345,-0.042924177,0.011300701,0.02687453,0.0060017104,-0.014904909,0.057561338,-0.01181294,0.09382724,0.02458935,-0.0065037077,0.007709675,-0.019299226,-0.024860432,-0.03363399,0.021035373,-0.054131612,-0.025896138,-0.0070999423,-0.030840987,0.022497233,-0.002224338,-0.03485398,-0.047332823,-0.045436054,0.02451575,0.02100323,-0.023318812,0.018998234,-0.05441183,-0.0706777,-0.046745844,0.06829461,-0.024030494,0.007857129,-0.010914368,-0.008974202,0.029852211,0.03436729,-0.02937871,0.06527389,0.027990116,0.055651825,-0.002090553,0.0800393,-0.049667608,0.00059321587,-0.004455433,0.01541718,0.04067046,0.08267731,0.031221082,-0.0026367859,0.043933757,0.03143183,-0.06217717,0.07580335,0.07250154,-0.049751367,0.048295975,0.01900352,0.0076094,-0.05551427,0.06487839,-0.019498853,-0.029371964,0.0169477,-0.0