247	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	72	document_chunk	2	The limitations associated with legacy decision support systems are that they lack agility to \nadjust to dynamic decision environments since they focus heavily on rigid processes like formal \nreporting methods and rules-based algorithms. They fail to capture and replicate tacit knowledge \nharvested from historical organizational decisions. As such, traditional DSS can not comprehend \nnatural language and therefore cannot be utilized by non-technical users. Above all, this \nlimitation points to the gap that necessitates continued efforts in intelligent knowledge-driven \nsolutions that aid context-based reasoning and decision-making. \n1.4 Knowledge Graphs as Structured Knowledge Representation	[0.030266488,0.06583001,-0.15714657,-0.04604278,0.04856506,0.033360057,0.0069073304,0.028142001,-0.00043081027,-0.020088252,0.036834795,0.0113381455,0.10606771,0.033086922,-0.008561085,-0.013572724,-0.075154155,-0.039113898,0.008712872,0.035323136,-0.006530843,-0.0073985355,-0.02475946,-0.035389405,0.015819773,0.02511453,0.0067886156,-0.030686405,-0.050792485,0.0057170345,0.067156546,0.060463067,0.03882463,-0.024604095,-0.04039015,-0.038155835,0.0740592,-0.043466263,0.0149089545,-0.012223439,-0.013955332,0.007709225,0.007925461,-0.056000587,0.07284326,-0.0100555485,0.06488443,-0.009696095,0.053547267,-0.04807034,0.002259105,-0.045936275,-0.01994265,0.018805422,0.0528216,-0.013740288,-0.04720997,0.06662348,0.024991842,-0.107636936,0.08980503,0.07388911,-0.05792197,0.04114926,0.011169067,-0.031762436,-0.027902579,0.0417952,-0.021553203,-0.04482082,0.01485216,0.0017663732,0.010764337,0.0052219457,-0.054331083,0.03085276,-0.03611221,-0.014459617,-0.039463952,0.077952966,-0.00015243358,-0.013237336,0.059760917,-0.03819757,0.048193138,0.0693434,-0.030902712,0.00925987,0.041856125,0.11095799,-0.010089113,0.0115843825,0.03702121,-0.0005780683,-0.067513496,0.05820175,-0.06782179,0.0031969345,-0.02455417,-0.022748299,-0.057771854,-0.03654825,-