276	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	80	document_chunk	2	Evidence 2: Peer-Reviewed: 91-Study Systematic Review of Knowledge Loss from Turnover \nFact: Past academic literature ascertains that the turnover of organizational staff members leads \nto quantifiable loss of routines, memory and absorptive ability. \nSource: A two-part synthesis of systematic literature published in The Learning Organization \n(Emerald Publishing) based on 91 empirical studies on knowledge loss induced by turnover \nfound that knowledge loss through turnover results in a wide range of organizational-level \neffects, such as the erosion of vital routines, organizational memory loss, and reduced absorptive \ncapacity. (Galan, 2023) (Galan, Knowledge loss induced by organizational member turnover: A \nreview of empirical literature, synthesis and future research directions (Part II), 2023) \nThe current state of decision support systems in colleges is mostly based on reports or isolated \ninformation systems, which are not aware of the historical context and cannot integrate \nstructured data with unstructured knowledge. These systems are not capable of providing the \nnecessary depth of analysis required for effective decision-making. This has made it difficult for \nthese institutions to learn from past decisions, which is critical in the decision-making process. \nWithout the use of a centralized and intelligent system for the preservation and organization of	[0.044269428,0.039172616,-0.1739458,-0.024073036,0.08136932,0.008422793,0.052378096,0.023774095,0.06505552,0.009309616,0.007399827,0.00595821,0.10127533,0.030721106,0.022893514,-0.04361323,-0.030368917,-0.03524614,-0.058535337,0.019581096,-0.013381051,-0.036403134,-0.044750333,-0.0082515,0.02214144,0.0562985,-0.025257979,-0.030900553,-0.03588312,0.019335901,0.052616417,0.020585142,0.034863275,-0.049037643,-0.080275364,-0.049386628,0.086688176,-0.016309576,0.028444594,-0.019353595,-0.0030368192,0.020354232,0.010832543,-0.048609328,0.034350958,0.04552303