305	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	87	document_chunk	1	Client-Side Functionality \nThe client side has input forms for decision context, which are arranged with the aim of \nuploading the supporting materials, thus ensuring good and accurate data acquisition. The client \nside has a natural language query, which allows the user interface with the decision-making \nsystem with the natural language, which does not require any technical skill. The client side \ndisplays the recommendations of the decision, as well as the cases in the history, with the aim of \nmaking an informed decision, thus enhancing transparency and enabling the user to know how \nthe conclusions can be made with the knowledge. \nServer-Side Functionality \nThe API services for the ingestion of the data and the retrieval of the same are high-performance \nasynchronous API services built with FastAPI. It supports integration and testing with API \ndocumentation. A hybrid approach is used for the storage of the data to utilize the capabilities of \nthe systems. For example, the structured data of the decision is stored by PostgreSQL, the \nknowledge graph is stored by Neo4j, and the vector store is used to determine the semantic \nsimilarities. It was decided to use this method rather than the database solution to achieve the \nbest performance. The selection of the applicable data sources and the reason paths is achieved \nby the application of the LLM-based routing and retrieval pipelines to the quality of the decision \nsupport. The knowledge graph constructions and queries are used to determine the insights based \non relationships that are hard to determine by relational databases. The workflows of LangGraph \nare used to control the state and the logic of the reasoning process. \nProject Accomplishments	[0.012896083,0.039876964,-0.15497649,-0.06864032,0.04671379,-0.06406656,0.026976584,-0.01818819,-0.040359784,-0.022262948,0.014177037,-6.242919e-05,0.09080639,0.0032193968,-0.030200448,-0.008485181,-0.031029876