316	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	92	document_chunk	0	The above diagram depicts a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) model, which can deal \nwith complex queries. It begins with the processing of the User Input by the first LLM, which \nrefines the input query. This is followed by the input query going through a Router. This router \nroutes the input query efficiently to the best possible data source, which could be a SQL DB, a \nKnowledge Graph (KG), or a Vector DB, based on the input query. When the information is \nretrieved after going through the process of Relevance Checking or Reranking, the final LLM \nproduces the Output. \n4. Summary of Milestones and Deliverables \nThe project will be developed using an iterative and modular approach. Key milestones and \ndeliverables are outlined below. \nMilestone \nNo. \nMilestone \nDeliverables \nStart \nDate \nEnd \nDate \nDuration Person \nResponsible \n1 \nGroup \nFormation and \nTopic \nFinalization \nFinalized team \nstructure and \napproved project \ntopic \n7 Jan \n2026 \n30 \nJan \n2026 \n24 days \nSamrat \n2 \nInitial Proposal \nDefense \nProposal presentation \nand feedback \n1 Feb \n2026 \n3 \nFeb \n2026 \n3 days \nALL \n3 \nProposal \nSubmission \nApproved written \nproject proposal \n4 Feb \n2026 \n10 \nFeb \n2026 \n7 days \nALL \n4 \nRequirement \nAnalysis and \nDetailed System \nDesign \nFunctional \nrequirements, system \narchitecture, data \nflow diagrams \n11 Feb \n2026 \n24 \nFeb \n2026 \n14 days \nSamrat	[0.0038439094,0.033515178,-0.20731029,-0.08117726,0.050762326,-0.044825066,0.024606341,0.020417864,-0.0026721978,-0.006964051,0.012658315,0.01188567,0.09884334,0.0225449,-0.024744732,-0.018475728,0.0154895745,-0.07122438,-0.05590603,0.036551986,-0.016229844,-0.033479385,-0.031194162,-0.019605987,0.01951561,-0.014320947,-0.0033281145,-0.045732543,-0.039254148,0.026507987,0.04406577,-0.03509346,-0.018582454,-0.053935073,-0.027774995,-0.04544121,0.058887593,-0.000938637,-0.0046585477,-0.033871178,0.029651936,-0.01