364	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	111	document_chunk	0	discovery to enhance \norganizational performance. \ncome up with valuable \nrecommendations that are aligned \nwith specific instances of \norganizational decisions. \nGutiérrez & Sequeda \n(2021) – Knowledge \nGraphs \nDefines knowledge graphs as \nsemantic graph-based models \nthat enhance the connectivity \nof the information and the \ncontextual representation of \nknowledge by modeling \nentities and relationships. \nOur project adopts the knowledge \ngraphs as the primary data modeling \nlayer in order to represent \norganizational procedures, policies, \nand situations of decisions. This can \nbe used to retrieve relationships and \nincreases explainability of decisions. \nChandak et al. (2022) – \nBuilding a Knowledge \nGraph for Precision \nMedicine \nShows how knowledge graphs \ncould be employed to aid \nclinical decision-making in \nhealthcare through the \ncombination of heterogeneous \nmedical data.  \nThough the focus of this paper was \non healthcare applications, our \nproject shows that the Knowledge \nGraph methodology is not only \nlimited to domain-specific medical \napplications but can also be applied \nto organizational decision \nenvironments. \nBader et al. (2020) – A \nKnowledge Graph for \nIndustry 4.0 \nDescribes how knowledge \ngraphs are being applied in \nmanufacturing to assist \nintelligent industrial decision \nsystems and combine \nproduction data. \nOur system extends the application \nof Knowledge Graphs outside of \nknowledge intensive organizational \ndecision support to industrial \nautomation. To be able to synthesize \ninformation and generate \nrecommendations, we integrate KG \nwith RAG-based generative AI. \nLewis et al. (2020) – \nRetrieval-Augmented \nGeneration for \nKnowledge-Intensive \nNLP Tasks \nIntroduces the RAG \narchitecture that integrates \nboth text generation and \ninformation retrieval to \nimprove contextual response \nas well as factual accuracy of \nNLP systems. \nKnowledge Graph-guided context \nenrichment and integration of \nstructured organizational data are \nused in our project to enhance the \nquality of retrieval and to keep RAG \nas the main reasoning mechanism. \nGao et al. (2023) – \nRetrieval-Augmented \nGives a detailed overview of \nRAG architectures and \noutlines the shortcomings, \nincluding the ability to retrieve \nOur system tries to resolve those \nlimitations by applying Knowledge \nGraph-based retrieval that enhances \nthe contextual understanding,	[0.029821662,0.08375919,-0.16607645,-0.04735034,0.04862937,-0.048348304,-0.021315366,0.0062388666,0.011101384,0.010971488,0.064631276,0.02209029,0.113751866,0.010310728,0.008595939,-0.005163582,-0.05500366,0.0015412654,-0.02376637,0.0006444806,-0.024414903,-0.020026738,-0.005951231,-0.029400127,0.010226675,0.0065962453,-0.007929324,-0.07157113,-0.04371921,0.016269399,0.012019456,0.019841133,0.01873158,-0.051957697,-0.0647218,-0.07319159,0.07457355,-0.010044804,0.016901335,0.012220031,-0.009939702,0.041261483,0.027893743,-0.05662031,0.04301604,0.022496564,0.030062633,-0.0023035526,0.050700646,-0.060481068,-0.012121254,0.0026463862,0.018493563,0.020393139,0.06499129,0.03028506,0.007511896,0.029777592,0.03127082,-0.07374455,0.09777308,0.08163191,-0.059352074,0.063771985,0.03855153,-0.016673738,-0.06622695,0.080363326,-0.007262143,-0.037643723,0.0047285147,-0.006879211,0.040802643,0.030396834,-0.03614245,0.028093401,-0.016492138,-0.0019970415,-0.007412815,0.077744104,0.03158249,0.010727176,0.060024176,-0.023884946,0.014398321,0.024165573,-0.048270524,-0.007879998,0.023518449,0.086038455,0.026118461,-0.0025105374,0.020325864,0.012868747,-0.065172516,0.06714412,-0.021589395,-0.011883674,-0.04640385,-0.020169778,-0.055663466,-0.040909406,-0.015267789,0.009409601,0.024524296,0.013983059,0.034100417,-0.015096569,0.001594819,0.014305324,-0.019020846,0.038779315,-0.019983225,0.026907401,-0.0030404145,0.017117772,0.06296481,-0.004712182,0.0124617275,0.04491834,0.0321