366	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	113	document_chunk	0	Generation for LLMs: A \nSurvey \nsingle document fragments \nwithout recording the semantic \nconnections between them. \nrelationship awareness, and multi-\nhop reasoning. \nWang et al. (2025) – \nConstruction of \nIntelligent Decision \nSupport Systems \n(IKEDS) \nIntroduces a smart DSS \narchitecture that combines AI \ntechniques with knowledge \nintegration and proves to be \nvery accurate across a variety \nof fields. \nThis framework is extended into our \nproject where modern LLM-based \nRAG architecture and Knowledge \nGraphs are incorporated to increase \nthe explainability, scalability, and \ndomain adaptability in a simulated \norganizational environment. \nZhu et al. (2025) – \nKnowledge Graph-\nGuided Retrieval \nAugmented Generation \n(KG2RAG) \nProposes KG-directed chunk \ngrowth procedures to enhance \nthe accuracy of retrieval and \nthe depth of reasoning, with \nbetter F1 scores in benchmark \nQA datasets. \nOur system uses KG-RAG \nintegration in a similar way but in \ndecision support cases rather than \nQA tasks and does not simply \nanswer questions but produces \nactionable recommendations. \nLi et al. (2025) – KA-\nRAG: Integrating \nKnowledge Graphs and \nAgentic Retrieval-\nAugmented Generation \nfor Intelligent \nEducational QA \nIntroduces the idea of an \neducational QA system \ncombining Knowledge Graphs \nwith agentic retrieval system, \nwhich can enhance a higher \nretrieval accuracy and domain-\nspecific question answering. \nKG-RAG methodology is applied to \norganizational DSS (and not \neducational QA) in our project. We \nconcentrate on strategic decision \nsupport, domain modeled knowledge \nand recommendation generation that \ncan be interacted with by the user. \nZhang et al. (2025) – \nGenerating Vicarious \nDialogue for Online \nLearning Using KG-RAG \nShows application of KG-\nenhanced RAG to create \ninteractive learning dialogue \nand creation of contextual \ncontent. \nKG-RAG is used in our system not \nin the educational dialogue but in the \nproduction of structured decision \nexplanations and recommendations \nin accordance with the \norganizational workflow. \nNguyen et al. (2024) – \nCross-Data Knowledge \nGraph Construction for \nEducational QA \nSystems \nPresents a system that uses \nmulti-source data integration \nto construct knowledge graphs \nin domains to provide \neducational answers to \nquestions. \nOur system expands the cross-data \nKG construction into simulated \norganizational datasets, combining \npolicies, operational data, and \nexternal knowledge sources to \nsupport decision making. \nZhang & Goyal (2024) – \nAI-Driven Decision \nIllustrates the importance of \nAI-based DSS in enhancing \nOur project extends DSS \nimplementation to non-higher	[0.009863217,0.07161837,-0.18175286,-0.076581314,0.0438911,-0.006540252,-0.01758887,0.021649634,-0.007559327,0.0069768066,0.04631761,0.010246083,0.12233406,0.025658194,-0.023813527,0.000111341345,-0.03673527,-0.018947782,-0.053292867,0.0066461996,-0.027091995,-0.027878406,-0.012165071,-0.04785628,0.05709706,-0.02194251,-0.027142586,-0.018353699,-0.03180959,-0.014294525,0.029269757,-0.022669168,0.03173931,-0.02861219,-0.06902186,-0.032182474,0.099599555,-0.025322966,-0.013305489,-0.00927365,0.011967489,-0.0024690037,0.041960694,-0.020760808,0.062344026,0.016822148,0.06882937,-0.0031673796,0.08799891,-0.047459014,-0.008153929,-0.02183793,0.03556256,0.042178746,0.06603326,0.04516271,-0.04492619,0.048458885,0.033814736,-0.068008825,0.07406263,0.045373313,-0.072069325,0.04573223,0.039687578,-0.030296901,-0.0645657,0.05684805,-0.039691053,-0.031192359,0.0189808,-0.012756575,0.030198442,0.045439918,-0.017580673,0.04684081,-0.0072448957,0.0006382783,0.0027888326,0.08806494,0.019417563,-0.013050237,0.065679215,-0.037060138,0.017912058,0.03388499,-0.037531875,0.010828923,0.008639793,0.060585923,0.010948575,0.030901322,0.030564,0.011517074,-0.07609689,0.05582606,-0.049720168,-0.029645415,