369	\N	12	\N	\N	\N	114	document_chunk	0	Support System \nInnovations to \nEmpower Higher \nEducation \nAdministration \nstrategic planning and \nresource allocation, as well as \nthe administrative decision-\nmaking process in higher \neducational institutions. \neducation sectors through a \nsimulated organizational setting, \nincluding Knowledge Graphs and \nRAG to enhance the general \ndecision-support. \nAbu Saa (2016) – \nEducational Data \nMining & Students’ \nPerformance Prediction \nShows how to use data mining \nmethods in predicting student \nperformance and enabling the \neducational decision-making \nprocess. \nOur project builds upon the \npredictive analytics by providing the \nconcepts of decision support on top \nof knowledge-based reasoning with \nAI, Knowledge Graphs, and RAG, \nand can offer explainable and \ncontext-aware decisions.  \nReferences \nAnon., 2022. Educational data mining: prediction of students’ academic performance using \nmachine learning algorithms. Smart learning environment, 9(11). \nAnon., 2025. The Importance and Applications of Decision Support Systems (DSS) in Higher \nEducation, s.l.: s.n. \nBader, S. e. a., 2020. A Knowledge Graph for Industry 4.0. In: C. B. T. B. S. Auer, ed. The \nSemantic Web – ISWC 2020. Cham: Springer: 465-480, p. 465–480. \nChandak, P. H. K. &. Z. M., 2022. Building a Knowledge Graph to Enable. bioRxiv, pp. 1-33. \nGaldamez, G., 2025. Using Knowledge Management to Minimize the Costs of Departing \nLeaders. [Online]  \nAvailable at: https://enterprise-knowledge.com/using-knowledge-management-to-minimize-the-\ncosts-of-departing-leaders/ \nGao, Y. e. a., 2023. Retrieval-Augmented Generation for LLMs: A Survey, s.l.: arXiv. \nGutiérrez, C. &. S. J., 2021. Knowledge Grapghs. Communications of the ACM, 64(63), p. 96–\n104. \nHak, P., Saddhono, K. & Pebriana, P., 2023. Integrating Decision Support Systems in Education: \nA Comprehensive Approach. AL-ISHLAH: Jurnal Pendidikan, 15(14), p. 4546–4552. \nHamou